  "hypothesis": "Integrating SoA storage (B) with NEON SIMD distance computation, max-heap top-k selection using global index tie-breaking for determinism (from A and B), OpenMP parallelization over groups with per-thread heaps and guided scheduling (C), and frequency array final label selection (A) will yield a correct and fast program. The key fix is accumulating per-thread heap across all assigned groups, which was missing in the previous incorrect integration.",
  "notes": "Fixed critical bug: local_size was reinitialized per group iteration due to being inside parallel for loop body; now declared outside omp for but inside parallel region so it accumulates correctly. Added global index tie-breaking (from source C) for deterministic merge when distances are equal. Used guided schedule as in source C. Precomputed start_idx array for global point order.",
